Pre-existing regression (unrelated to NEARS-3630, environment-level Firebase
misconfig — same root cause family as the already-documented
bug-logout-firebase-failure.log from the fix-cycle 1 full QA pass).

Observed during delta re-QA fix-cycle 2, attempting to log in as
james.wilson@demo.com (a real-photo seeded account) to regression-check the
photo-path of MenuProfileHeaderCard live: AuthController.login() ->
AuthService.login() -> AuthService._updateHeaderFunctionality() ->
AuthRepository.updateToken() calls FirebaseMessaging.instance, which throws
because Firebase is not initialized in this dev environment
([core/no-app] No Firebase App '[DEFAULT]' has been created). The exception
IS logged via a paired AppLogger failure line (FcmTokenFetchFailure, PII-safe,
satisfies the logging contract's "no silent failure" rule) but then escapes
uncaught past that point, aborting the remainder of AuthController.login()'s
work for that call. Effects observed:
  - 1st and 2nd Sign In taps: login appeared to no-op (POST /api/v1/auth/login
    returned 200, but the app never navigated off the sign-in screen).
  - 3rd Sign In tap: navigation to Home succeeded, but the SAME exception
    fired ~3s later, apparently having interrupted whatever step populates
    ProfileController.userInfoModel for this session — the merged Profile
    screen (menu_screen.dart, both entry points) was left in a permanent
    isLoading=true skeleton state (grey avatar, no name, no stat cards),
    per menu_screen.dart's `isLoading: isLoggedIn && !hasError &&
    profileController.userInfoModel == null` — never resolved even ~30s
    later.
  - Edit Profile (update_profile_screen.dart) for the SAME account loaded
    correctly (own independent data path) and rendered the name "James
    Wilson" plus an attempted-photo state (image icon placeholder, since
    the actual seed image file does not exist on disk in this dev
    environment per NEARS-1092 — a separate, already-documented worktree
    limitation) rather than initials, confirming update_profile_screen.dart's
    `!userInfoModel.hasNoPhoto` gate correctly took the photo branch for a
    real-photo account.

Live logcat excerpt (emulator-5556, pid 11032):
